# fstab for the mt6877 platform (common to all mt6877 devices).
#
# Reconstruction of the realme 11 Pro 5G stock fstab, reduced to what is true of
# the platform. Source: /vendor/etc/fstab on the device, plus the EROFS
# odm/etc/oplus.fstab from the stock A13 OTA.
#
# WHAT IS PLATFORM vs WHAT IS DEVICE
#   platform: the logical partition layout (system/vendor/product/odm/system_ext)
#             and the first-stage mount flags.
#   device:   partition SIZES, the super group name, the AVB pubkey path, and
#             any device-specific mount (nvdata, protect1/2, persist...).
# Those device-specific lines are deliberately NOT here. Copy the device's own
# fstab in, do not inherit one.
#
# Two realme specifics that are NOT platform facts and are therefore absent:
#   * the my_* regional logical partitions (my_company, my_region, my_heytap,
#     my_carrier, ...) -- an OPPO/realme regional split, not a chipset trait
#   * /mnt/vendor/protect1, protect2, nvdata, nvcfg -- realme security storage

system        /system        ext4  ro,barrier=1  wait,logical,first_stage_mount
vendor        /vendor        ext4  ro,barrier=1  wait,logical,first_stage_mount
product       /product       ext4  ro,barrier=1  wait,logical,first_stage_mount
system_ext    /system_ext    ext4  ro,barrier=1  wait,logical,first_stage_mount
odm           /odm           ext4  ro,barrier=1  wait,logical,first_stage_mount

# The stock A13 images are EROFS (magic 0xe0f5e1e2), not ext4. The platform
# ships ext4 lines because that is what an AOSP-built super uses; a device that
# mounts the stock EROFS partitions instead overrides this file with its own.

# Device-specific mount points. Each device tree supplies these; they are listed
# here only as a checklist of what a device fstab is likely to need, NOT as
# active lines:
#   /dev/block/by-name/metadata    /metadata
#   /dev/block/by-name/userdata     /data         (f2fs on this device)
#   /dev/block/by-name/nvdata       /mnt/vendor/nvdata
#   /dev/block/by-name/protect1     /mnt/vendor/protect_f
#   /dev/block/by-name/protect2     /mnt/vendor/protect_s
#   /dev/block/by-name/persist      /mnt/vendor/persist